# Platform Ops

Use this when the user asks to inspect or change machine settings, desktop behavior, hardware preferences, native app settings, or OS services.

## Current Target
{{ template "codex/current-target.md.tmpl" . }}

## Scope Decision

- Shared and durable: edit `~/src/boilerplate/home/...`, sync the same files into `~/.local/share/chezmoi/home/...`, then apply with `chezmoi`.
- Machine-local and OS-owned: change the live OS or app setting directly on the target host.
- Home router/firewall/DHCP/DNS on `10.77.77.1`: use the `opnsense` skill and `opnsense-api`. Do not use computer-use or raw `curl -k`.

## Shared vs Local

- Shared: shell, tmux, OMP, Codex Desktop, Ghostty, Kitty, Hyprland, Waybar, Mako, Walker, and user services shipped in the boilerplate.
- Machine-local: trackpad speed, keyboard repeat rate, display scaling, battery policy, Bluetooth pairings, and app login state.
- If unclear, inspect where the current value lives before editing.

## Omarchy And Linux

- Package installs: `omarchy-pkg-add`.
- Inspect `hyprctl devices`, relevant `hyprctl getoption` values, and systemd unit status before changing them.
- Durable desktop config lives under `~/src/boilerplate/home/dot_config/`; the corresponding live files are under `~/.config/`.
- Validate Hyprland changes with `hyprctl reload` and `hyprctl configerrors`.
- Treat Omarchy desktop changes as shared only when they belong in the normal workstation baseline.

## macOS

- Shared CLI and dotfile behavior goes through `brew`, `mise`, and `chezmoi`.
- Native preferences usually stay machine-local unless the user explicitly wants them standardized.
- Inspect before writing with `defaults`, `pmset`, `scutil`, `networksetup`, `systemsetup`, or `launchctl` as appropriate.
- Prefer CLI changes when they are clear and reversible. If a setting is UI-only, say so instead of guessing.
- Avoid user-facing UI changes on `macmini` unless explicitly requested; treat it as server-first.

## Reliability Rules

- Inspect before writing and decide shared versus local first.
- Keep machine-local state out of shared agent guidance unless it is durable and portable.
- Re-read changed settings or files after writing.
- For shared changes, verify the rendered live file after a targeted chezmoi apply.

## Home Network

- The LAN gateway is OPNsense at `https://10.77.77.1`.
- Read `skill://opnsense` and use `opnsense-api` for appliance changes.
- Client/host network settings (macOS `networksetup`, Tailscale, DNS on this machine) stay in this skill.
